.TH _NIME 1 "2026-11" "_nime 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
_nime \- browse and watch anime from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B _nime
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIquery\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B _nime
searches an anime streaming site, lists the episodes, resolves the stream and
hands it to a local player. It scrapes
.BR animesuge.cz " and " anichan.to
and talks to the MegaPlay player directly, including its encrypted stream
payload, which it decrypts with
.BR openssl (1).
.PP
When no player is available it prints the stream url, the subtitle url and the
required referer instead of failing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-source " \fIname\fR"
Source to use: \fIanimesuge\fR (default) or \fIanichan\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-continue
Continue watching from history.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-download
Download the episode instead of playing it, with
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
or
.BR ffmpeg (1).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-delete
Delete the history file and exit.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-episode " \fIn\fR"
Play episode \fIn\fR, or a range such as \fI1\-3\fR.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-range " \fIn\fR"
Same as \fB\-\-episode\fR.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quality " \fIq\fR"
Quality to pick: \fIbest\fR (default), \fIworst\fR, or a height such as
\fI1080\fR.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-select\-nth " \fIn\fR"
Select the nth search result or history entry without opening a menu.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-vlc
Use VLC instead of mpv.
.TP
.B \-\-dub
Play the dubbed version, when the source has one.
.TP
.BR \-\-sub\-lang " \fIlang\fR"
Subtitle track to use, as a language code (\fIeng\fR, \fIger\fR, \fIspa\fR) or
as a name (\fIgerman\fR). With \fB\-\-download\fR, \fIall\fR embeds every
track the source offers. Without it the track the source marks default is used.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-subs
Print the subtitle tracks available for the selected episode, with language
codes, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-skip
Skip the opening and the ending. Works by writing a small mpv script with the
intro and outro marks the player reports. mpv only.
.TP
.B \-\-syncplay
Play through Syncplay, so playback can be shared with other people.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-detach
Keep the player in the foreground instead of backgrounding it.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-deps
Print the state of every required and optional dependency, the detected
player and the default source, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-update
Fetch the script from the git repository, compare versions and replace the
installed copy, keeping the previous one as \fI_nime.bak\fR.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B _NIME_SOURCE
Default source.
.TP
.B _NIME_MODE
\fIsub\fR or \fIdub\fR.
.TP
.B _NIME_QUALITY
Default quality.
.TP
.B _NIME_PLAYER
Player command to use instead of the detected one.
.TP
.B _NIME_PLAYER_FLAGS
Extra flags handed to the player.
.TP
.B _NIME_MENU
\fIfzf\fR (default) or \fInone\fR for a numbered prompt.
.TP
.B _NIME_HIST_DIR
Directory holding the history file. Defaults to
\fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/_nime\fR.
.TP
.B _NIME_DOWNLOAD_DIR
Directory downloads are written to. Defaults to a folder named
\fI_nime downloads\fR inside the XDG download dir, \fI~/Downloads\fR,
\fI~/Desktop\fR or the home directory, whichever exists first.
.TP
.B _NIME_SKIP
Set to \fI1\fR to always skip intros and outros.
.TP
.B _NIME_SUB_LANG
Default subtitle language.
.TP
.B _NIME_COLOR
Set to \fI0\fR to disable colours.
.TP
.B _NIME_USER ", " _NIME_BRANCH
Repository and branch used by \fB\-U\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/_nime/nime-hsts
History: one tab separated line per anime, holding the episode, the source, the
id and the title.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/_nime/nime-skip.lua
Generated mpv script used by \fB\-\-skip\fR.
.TP
.I <download folder>/_nime downloads/
Where \fB\-\-download\fR writes. Files are mp4 with the subtitles muxed in as a
selectable soft track.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Search and play interactively:
.EX
_nime frieren
.EE
.TP
Play episode five in 1080p:
.EX
_nime \-q 1080 \-e 5 frieren
.EE
.TP
Watch the other source with intros skipped:
.EX
_nime \-\-skip \-s anichan frieren
.EE
.TP
Continue from history:
.EX
_nime \-c
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error, including a failed search, a missing player, a
failed decryption or an episode that could not be resolved.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR openssl (1),
.BR mpv (1),
.BR vlc (1),
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
